module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_dispatch_surface_probe_asserts_generated_text_not_its_derivation

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// THREE SURVIVING RED CLAIMS were enrolled here, named by their actual causes, held until the repair
// owned by work item adhoc-972c2336-4c5 lands. STANDING CORRECTED 2026-10-27 (fierce-ferret-64, node
// adhoc-0201be55-56b): of the three, SURVIVING RED 3 (printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable)
// is CLOSED -- it was measured GREEN on main, its stale spark_* roster had already been dropped by
// #15160, and it has now been re-expressed as a read of the closed roster, the mode-to-job assignment
// and the emitted job list, with its own RED and positive-control receipts below. REDS 1 AND 2 ARE
// CLOSED TOO, and this row's declared trigger capability has therefore FIRED for all three named
// claims: #14717 c126037f0b2 (merged 2026-10-27 08:47Z) re-expressed both
// trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision probes as reads of the derivation, through the
// new shared predicate test.claim.fleet.fleet_converge_checkout_trust, and both measure PASS on main
// (receipt below). WHAT IS LEFT STALE IS THIS ROW'S OWN STANDING, and it is named here rather than
// papered over: its rung line still reads BelowCeiling { blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt } with a trigger
// naming a capability the corpus NOW HAS -- the exact dangling state
// gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.declared_frontier_outlives_the_firing_of_its_own_trigger describes. The
// row's repair-owner receipt says it retires when the trigger fires; retiring it (deleting the row file,
// precedent #14197, the claims staying enrolled as regression controls) is a separate operation this
// node's assignment does not cover, so the row is left enrolled with the firing recorded and the
// retirement routed to the manager.
// The three are NOT regressions introduced by the re-contract of
// the three trusted-checkout claims (that re-contract turned test.claim.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_run_witness
// green, 39 -> 40 at the branch head); they are PRE-EXISTING reds measured identical at the branch
// base and at the branch head -- a control run at the base (dispatch ctl14, fresh build) and at the
// head (dispatch claimrun tables) report the same three failures on the same conjuncts, so nothing
// this PR does widens them, and the manager's side-chat ruling requires they carry a typed
// declaration naming their causes and a capability-based repair trigger rather than silence.

data a_dispatch_surface_probe_asserts_generated_text_not_its_derivation: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_dispatch_surface_probe_asserts_generated_text_not_its_derivation" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "THE CAPABILITY THAT WOULD LET THIS ROW RETIRE: a mechanical check that refuses a fleet-converge dispatch-surface claim whose asserted text is a literal of the EMITTED workflow -- an options-list element or an if-condition clause -- rather than a read of the derivation that text is generated from. CORRECTED 2026-10-27 (node adhoc-0201be55-56b): the trigger this row carried on 2026-10-25 -- re-expressing the three claims it named -- HAS FIRED and is recorded as fired: claim 3 by #15245 (the printer witness now reads fleet_converge_workflow_modes, fleet_converge_spark_target_modes, fleet_converge_mode_job_id and fleet_converge_jobs) and claims 1 and 2 by #14717 c126037f0b2 (both trusted_code probes now read the per-job checkout ref and the derived shared-job condition through test.claim.fleet.fleet_converge_checkout_trust). Hand re-expression discharges the three enrollments; it does not reach the ceiling, because the class is still writable and nothing refuses it -- which is why blocker stays ClimbableButUnbuilt and ceiling stays MechanicallyPreventable. See the row's own declared_frontier_outlives_the_firing_of_its_own_trigger for the failure mode this correction is avoiding." } },

  receipts: [
    "**THE DEFECT:** a dispatch-surface probe asserts a literal substring of the EMITTED workflow text (an exclusion clause of the shared job's if-condition) or a literal roster of mode options, instead of reading the derivation those texts come from. When the derivation is legitimately re-shaped, the probe goes red on a true program. This is the same class gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.workflow_job_selection_diverges_from_mode_assignment closed for the shared job's own condition (#13607, 2026-10-09): the repair then MADE the shared job's if a positive derivation from fleet_converge_mode_job_id over the closed mode roster -- which is exactly what silently reddened the probes that kept asserting the retired NEGATIVE exclusion spelling.",
    "**SURVIVING RED 1, test.claim.namecheap_workflow_witness.trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision:** its fourth conjunct demands fleet_converge_shared_job_if contain \"github.event.inputs.mode != 'namecheap_observe'\". Since the #13607 re-derivation the shared job's if carries positive selectors only; namecheap_observe has its OWN dedicated job (emitted fleet-converge.yml: job 'namecheap_observe' with if github.event.inputs.mode == 'namecheap_observe'), so the negative clause the probe greps for no longer exists anywhere. The claim's first three conjuncts (the dispatch-revision ref expression, the event-sha arm, the absence of expected_revision) all hold. Cause: derivation re-shape (#13607 repair), not a lost security property.",
    "**SURVIVING RED 2, test.claim.printer_workflow_binding_witness.trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision:** identical shape -- its fourth conjunct demands fleet_converge_shared_job_if contain \"github.event.inputs.mode != 'printer'\"; printer likewise has its own dedicated emitted job (if github.event.inputs.mode == 'printer'), so the negative clause is gone. Its first three conjuncts hold.",
    "**SURVIVING RED 3, test.claim.printer_workflow_binding_witness.printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable: CLOSED 2026-10-27 (node adhoc-0201be55-56b, fierce-ferret-64).** It demanded every one of eleven named modes appear exactly once in fleet_converge_mode_options. Four (printer, workspace_commissioning_plan, r2_workspace_object_read_mint, r2_workspace_object_write_mint) do; the seven spark_* names (spark_runtime_image_produce, spark_runtime_image_distribute, spark_arm_checkpoint_materialize, spark_arm_group_observe, spark_arm_group_launch_plan, spark_arm_group_launch, spark_arm_group_load) were REMOVED from FleetConvergeWorkflowMode by fa44b9810259 (2026-10-10, v1 closeout mega branch #13641) and their modes left the emitted options list. Cause: retired-mode roster, not a lost dispatch capability for the four surviving modes.",
    "**RED 3 IS NOT RED ON MAIN -- the standing was stale, measured 2026-10-27.** claim_batch --wet --functions at origin/main ae563700cbe (dispatch 2026-10-26 20:12 UTC, fresh build) prints PASS printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable. The eleven-name roster was repaired by c62131787d3 (#15160, 2026-10-26, 'printer witness: drop the 7 modes #13641 retired from the dispatchable-modes list'), which is an ancestor of main; the four surviving names each appear exactly once in the 74-element fleet_converge_mode_options, which matches the emitted .github/workflows/fleet-converge.yml option list element for element. The guess that a lost excluded_from_dispatch filter caused it is FALSE on main: the filter is live in gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_workflow fleet_converge_dispatchable_modes -- `filter(fleet_converge_workflow_modes, m => count(fleet_converge_spark_target_options) > 0 || !fleet_converge_mode_is_spark_target_mode(mode: m))`, where fleet_converge_mode_is_spark_target_mode reads fleet_converge_spark_target_modes -- and it is ACTIVE today: the closed roster carries 81 modes, 7 of them spark_* (SparkGrants, SparkBootstrap, SparkServingApply, SparkNativeServingApply, SparkRuntimeImageProbe, SparkWirelessLinkConverge, SparkGrantsObserve), and they are exactly the 7 the filter drops to reach 74.",
    "**REDS 1 AND 2 ARE CLOSED, AND THEY WERE CLOSED BY A DIFFERENT REPAIR THAN THIS ROW ENVISIONED -- measured 2026-10-27.** #14717 c126037f0b2 (merged 2026-10-27 08:47Z, 'Checkout-trust witnesses assert the per-job ref rule (boot, printer, namecheap)') deleted each witness's hand-written fourth conjunct -- the one demanding fleet_converge_shared_job_if spell `mode != 'namecheap_observe'` / `mode != 'printer'` -- and moved the assertion into the new shared predicate test.claim.fleet.fleet_converge_checkout_trust, which asserts the per-job checkout refs by EQUALITY against the emitted expressions and derives the shared job's mode set as `fleet_converge_shared_job_if == fleet_converge_any_mode_step_if(filter(fleet_converge_workflow_modes, mode => fleet_converge_mode_job_id(mode: mode) == fleet_converge_shared_job_id && mode != excluded))`. That is this row's own named repair: a read of the mode-to-job assignment and the closed roster, not a substring of the emitted if-condition. MEASURED ON MAIN with #14717 present: PASS trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision in BOTH witnesses (claim_batch --wet --functions, invocation 0d80855d-bd3e-4437-88f2-6677b8b3ebe1 at head 5ac7c07b262, which carries c126037f0b2). NOTE ON A MISREADING THAT NEARLY MISSED IT: an earlier run at origin/main c2a6f632dc6 reported those same two probes FAILING, but not from their own conjuncts -- the whole closure failed to resolve on dag/product/fabric/serving_recipe.dag:127:7 'non-exhaustive match: missing variant(s) WeightsPinnedAtHub', a break #15222 468d6f57051 landed on main and #15257 27d1dc4d109 (merged 2026-10-27 18:04Z) fixed. A claim that cannot resolve reports FAIL, so a resolve break upstream is indistinguishable from a red claim in that output: check the diagnostic line, not the verdict word.",
    "**RED 3 CHAIN RE-DERIVATION (§6b): the CLAIM was stale, the product lost nothing -- but the claim was still this row's defect.** fa44b9810259's own message justifies the retirement ('every Spark sold... GitHub Actions rejects a workflow_dispatch input whose options list is empty, so the dead option goes with the fleet'), and no dag file anywhere still names the seven retired variants (grep over dag/: zero hits for each). So the eleven-name list was asserting retired modes, and #15160 corrected it. What remained unjustified is the SHAPE: it asserted a literal roster of wire names out of fleet_converge_mode_options, the generated input-choice projection, which is this row's own named defect. Repaired at that boundary: the witness now reads the closed roster in the mode's typed value (membership in fleet_converge_workflow_modes, non-exclusion by fleet_converge_spark_target_modes, exactly-once in the projection, and REACHABILITY through fleet_converge_mode_job_id into the emitted fleet_converge_jobs() list the yml is written from).",
    "**RED 3 RECEIPT, re-measured in a SINGLE remote dispatch against ONE checked-out head (claim_batch --wet --functions; the earlier per-row dispatches at 02:30/02:59/03:28/03:48 UTC are superseded -- they ran before the branch was rebased onto main, so they did not all run at the shipped head).** The dispatch mutates the PRODUCT in-run, never the claim, and injects the EXACT body this claim carried at origin/main ae563700cbe as a throwaway witness (legacy_projection_probe_shape) so the old shape and the new one are measured under the same mutation in the same run. GREEN: PASS printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable, PASS spark_target_exclusion_filter_is_live, PASS legacy_projection_probe_shape, PASS trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision x2 (both witnesses). RED (A), fleet_converge_printer_job() deleted from fleet_converge_jobs() -- the mode stays listed and selectable but lands no job: FAIL printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable, PASS legacy_projection_probe_shape. THE PROJECTION CANNOT SEE A LOST JOB: the old shape passes the mutation this row exists to catch, in the same invocation as the new shape fails it. RED (B), R2WorkspaceObjectWriteMint listed twice in fleet_converge_workflow_modes (roster 81 -> 82, options 74 -> 75): FAIL printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable, and the old shape FAILS it too (it counted options too), which is expected -- B is not the discriminating case, A is. POSITIVE CONTROL: spark_target_exclusion_filter_is_live PASSes green AND under both mutations, so the exclusion conjunct is not vacuous and the control is not collateral damage. (Two dispatches carried this because one invocation exceeded the runner's 45-minute cap before run B; verdict lines are identical in kind and both ran against the same tree.)",
    "**MEASURED, not inferred:** control dispatch ctl14 at branch base f4619452d9922c0ec9ce16a5ce8a2cce7470f09a (fresh build) reports namecheap 3/4 and printer 4/6 with exactly these failing names; the same run at the branch head reports the identical set, while mtcollins1_boot_run_witness moves 39/40 -> 40/40 (the re-contract's own RED -> GREEN). The three reds are therefore pre-existing main-side drift on other conjuncts, visible in the claim tables, un-enrolled before this row.",
    "**REPAIR OWNER:** work item adhoc-972c2336-4c5 (filed by the manager 2026-10-25). When the repair lands -- the three claims re-expressed as reads of fleet_converge_mode_job_id and the closed mode roster -- this row's trigger capability has fired and this row retires with it; the claims remain as ordinary regression controls.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.namecheap_workflow_witness", decl_name: "trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.printer_workflow_binding_witness", decl_name: "trusted_code_cannot_be_replaced_by_dispatch_revision", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.printer_workflow_binding_witness", decl_name: "printer_and_main_workspace_modes_remain_dispatchable", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_workflow", decl_name: "fleet_converge_shared_job_if", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_workflow", decl_name: "fleet_converge_mode_job_id", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
